 to boost sprinting last but not  least look for armor that enhances  sprinting and sliding both of which go a  long way and making you hard to kill  this leads us to the shadow shot super  on its own the super isn't lethal but it  restricts your foes movements and  abilities making them vulnerable to your  friends in your own follow-up attacks  whether alone or in a group the true  power of the shadow shot is harnessed  through your passive abilities under the  way of the trapper you can enhance the  super with deadfall which unleashes void  anchor traps when choosing way of the  pathfinder the möbius quiver can  transform the shadow shot into a  damage-dealing super part of the pack  which conjures orbs of light as you kill  underscores the supers usefulness  against multiple enemies as opposed to a  single boss  last but not least don't get mail a  cocky combination blow one of the way of  the warrior passive abilities triggers  health regeneration and increases melee  damage and this boost can feel  empowering but you're not invincible it  can be easy to get caught in a killing  spree and ignore your low health this  also applies to the arc staff just  because you have the superhuman ability  to disintegrate your foes doesn't mean  you're impervious to attacks especially  when your staff can't reach far-off  enemies  and those are our tips for hunter  optimization the beauty of destiny 2 is  that there will be countless raids  strikes and other post story skirmishes  to hone your hunter skills we encourage  you to give each subclass a shot you  might be surprised what you'll discover  after spending a dozen hours of the  Night Stalker even if you're more  comfortable with say the arc Strider  thanks for watching

